{
  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "SOP-SEC-01-sec-1",
      "sop_id": "SOP-SEC-01",
      "title": "Phishing & Social Engineering Incident Response Procedure",
      "section": "1.0 Initial Identification & Triage",
      "content": "- Extract full RFC 822 internet headers, recipient list, sending MTA IP, SPF/DKIM/DMARC authentication results.\n- Identify all Indicators of Compromise (IoCs): malicious URLs, embedded tracking pixels, attachment hashes (SHA-256).\n- If the email contains a credential harvesting hyperlink, query SIEM proxy/DNS telemetry to check for active clicks by internal users.",
      "keywords": [
        "users.",
        "recipient",
        "indicators",
        "tracking",
        "credential",
        "harvesting",
        "embedded",
        "authentication",
        "contains",
        "urls",
        "internal",
        "sending",
        "pixels",
        "siem",
        "proxy"
      ],
      "embedding": null
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "SOP-SEC-01-sec-2",
      "sop_id": "SOP-SEC-01",
      "title": "Phishing & Social Engineering Incident Response Procedure",
      "section": "2.0 Containment Protocol",
      "content": "- Step 2.1: Submit sender domain and source IP to corporate perimeter firewall and mail gateway blocklists (block SMTP/TLS inbound).\n- Step 2.2: Purge the malicious email from all recipient inboxes using M365 Security & Compliance / Google Workspace Admin quarantine API.\n- Step 2.3: For any user who clicked the hyperlink or submitted credentials:\n    a) Force immediate active session revocation across all IdP tokens (Okta / Azure AD / PingFederate).\n    b) Reset active Active Directory / LDAP account passwords.\n    c) Enforce MFA re-enrollment and review registered MFA devices for rogue FIDO2/TOTP tokens.",
      "keywords": [
        "compliance",
        "submit",
        "m365",
        "google",
        "containment",
        "recipient",
        "admin",
        "domain",
        "purge",
        "revocation",
        "api.",
        "blocklists",
        "enforce",
        "sender",
        "fido2"
      ],
      "embedding": null
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "SOP-SEC-01-sec-3",
      "sop_id": "SOP-SEC-01",
      "title": "Phishing & Social Engineering Incident Response Procedure",
      "section": "3.0 Eradication & Remediation",
      "content": "- Step 3.1: Null-route malicious domains at corporate DNS Sinkhole resolvers (0.0.0.0).\n- Step 3.2: If attachment execution occurred, isolate affected endpoints from VLAN immediately via EDR host isolation.\n- Step 3.3: Run deep memory and persistence inspection (Registry Run keys, Scheduled Tasks, WMI event subscriptions).",
