      ],
      "embedding": null
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "SOP-SEC-02-sec-2",
      "sop_id": "SOP-SEC-02",
      "title": "Ransomware & Destructive Malware Containment Procedure",
      "section": "2.0 Urgent Containment Protocol",
      "content": "- Step 2.1: Immediately isolate host via EDR network containment. Do NOT power down or reboot the machine to preserve volatile RAM memory for forensic acquisition.\n- Step 2.2: Sever SMB/RPC interconnects at core switches between affected subnet and central file servers (port 445 / 139 / 135 block).\n- Step 2.3: Freeze administrative service accounts exhibiting anomalous lateral movement in Active Directory.\n- Step 2.4: Verify offline immutability of volume shadow backups and enterprise storage snapshots; disable cloud backup sync agents to prevent encrypted file sync.",
      "keywords": [
        "movement",
        "sync",
        "prevent",
        "agents",
        "lateral",
        "containment",
        "network",
        "switches",
        "servers",
